# {{lb|en|uncountable}}
## The amount of space between points (often geographical points), usually (but not necessarily) measured along a straight line.
##: {{ux|en|The '''distance''' to Petersborough is thirty miles.}}
##: {{ux|en|From Moscow, the '''distance''' is relatively short to Saint Petersburg, relatively long to Novosibirsk, but even greater to Vladivostok.}}
### {{lb|en|boxing}}
#### The [[maximum#Adjective|maximum]] amount of space between a [[boxer]] and their [[opponent#Noun|opponent]] within which the boxer can [[punch#Verb|punch]] [[effectively]].
#### ''Often in'' '''[[go the distance]]''''','' '''[[last#Verb|last]] the distance''''', or'' '''[[stay the distance]]''': the [[scheduled#Adjective|scheduled]] duration of a [[bout#Noun|bout]].
### {{lb|en|fencing}} The amount of space between a [[fencer]] and their opponent, which the fencer [[try#Verb|tries]] to [[control#Verb|control]] in order to [[gain#Verb|gain]] an [[advantage#Noun|advantage]] over the opponent.
###* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merry Wives|act=II|scene=i|page=45|column=1|passage={{quote-gloss|''William''}} ''Page''. I haue heard the French-man hath good skill in his Rapier. / [[w:Robert Shallow|{{quote-gloss|''Robert''}} ''Shal''&#91;''low''&#93;]]. Tut ſir: I could haue told you more: In theſe times you ſtand on '''diſtance''': your Paſſes, Stoccado's, and I knovv not vvhat: {{...}}}}
### {{lb|en|horse racing}} Originally, the space measured back from the [[winning post]] which a racehorse [[run#Verb|running]] in a [[heat#Noun|heat]] must [[reach#Verb|reach]] when the [[winner]] has [[cover#Verb|covered]] the [[whole#Adjective|whole]] [[course#Noun|course]], in order to run in a [[subsequent#Adjective|subsequent]] heat; also, the point on the racecourse that space away from the winning post; now, the point on a racecourse 240 yards from the winning post.
###* {{RQ:L'Estrange Fables of Aesop|fablenumber=CCCXXXIX|fable=A Plain Horse Wins the Prize|page=296|passage=THere vvere a Great many Brave, Sightly ''Horſes'' vvith Rich Trappings that vvere brought out One day to the Courſe, and Only ''One Plain Nag'' in the Company that made ſport for All the reſt. But vvhen they came at laſt to the Tryal, ''This'' vvas the ''Horſe'' that ran the VVhole Field out of '''Diſtance''', and VVon the Race. / The MORAL. ''Our Senſes are No Competent Judges of the Excellencies of the Mind.''}}
### {{lb|en|military}} The amount of space between [[soldier#Noun|soldiers]] or [[cavalry]] [[rider]]s [[march#Verb|marching]] or [[stand#Verb|standing]] in a [[rank#Noun|rank]]; also, the amount of space between such ranks.
### {{lb|en|sport}} The [[complete#Adjective|complete]] length of a course over which a race is run.
## ''Chiefly preceded by'' '''[[the#Article|the]]''''', especially in'' '''[[into]]''' ''or'' '''[[in the distance]]''': the place that is far away or remote.
